.TH BITLOG 3 "May 2026" "C99 Bitlog Library" "Linux Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
bitlog \- ultra-lightweight, fixed-size bit array tracking system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "bitlog.h"
.HP
.B typedef struct { ... } bitlog_t;
.HP
.BI "int bitlog_word_count_for_bits(uint64_t " bits ");"
.HP
.BI "int bitlog_is_empty(const bitlog_t *" log ");"
.HP
.BI "int bitlog_init(bitlog_t *" log ", uint64_t *" buffer ", int " word_count ");"
.HP
.BI "int bitlog_test(const bitlog_t *" log ", uint64_t " index ");"
.HP
.BI "void bitlog_set(bitlog_t *" log ", uint64_t " index ");"
.HP
.BI "void bitlog_clear(bitlog_t *" log ", uint64_t " index ");"
.HP
.BI "int bitlog_pop_lowest(bitlog_t *" log ");"
.HP
.BI "int bitlog_pop_highest(bitlog_t *" log ");"
.HP
.BI "uint64_t bitlog_get_used_count(const bitlog_t *" log ");"
.HP
.BI "void bitlog_clear_all(bitlog_t *" log ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bitlog
is a single-header, zero-allocation C99 utility designed to manage a compact 
bit array backed by a user-provided buffer of 64-bit words. It provides 
constant-time metadata tracking, including population counts and active slot 
boundaries, allowing aggressive compiler optimizations and fast bit manipulation.
.PP
The internal tracking structures minimize scanning overhead during prioritized 
extractions, making it highly suitable for high-performance scheduling, tracking, 
or event logs.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BI bitlog_word_count_for_bits( bits )
Calculates the number of 64-bit words required to safely hold the specified number 
of 
.I bits
without integer overflow. Returns the word count, or -1 if the result would 
overflow an integer.
.TP
.BI bitlog_is_empty( log )
Returns a non-zero value if the bit log contains no set bits, and 0 otherwise. 
Executes in
.I O(1)
time.
.TP
.BI bitlog_init( log ", " buffer ", " word_count )
Initializes the 
.I bitlog_t
structure to manage the provided memory 
.I buffer
consisting of
.I word_count
elements. It scans existing data to accurately construct internal tracking hints and 
population counts. Returns 0 on success, or -1 if inputs are invalid.
.TP
.BI bitlog_test( log ", " index )
Tests the bit at the specified
.I index\fR.
Aborts via 
.BR assert (3)
if the index maps out of bounds. Returns non-zero if the bit is set, and 0 otherwise.
.TP
.BI bitlog_set( log ", " index )
Sets the bit at the specified
.I index
to 1. Tracks internal boundary changes and increments the total population count if 
the bit was not previously set. Bounds are enforced via
.BR assert (3).
.TP
.BI bitlog_clear( log ", " index )
Clears the bit at the specified
.I index
to 0. Dynamically tightens search boundaries and decrements the tracking counts. 
Bounds are enforced via
.BR assert (3).
.TP
.BI bitlog_pop_lowest( log )
Finds, clears, and returns the absolute bit index of the lowest set bit in the log. 
Optimized using the hardware instruction
.BR __builtin_ctzll (3).
Returns -1 if the log is empty.
.TP
.BI bitlog_pop_highest( log )
Finds, clears, and returns the absolute bit index of the highest set bit in the log. 
Optimized using the hardware instruction
.BR __builtin_clzll (3).
Returns -1 if the log is empty.
.TP
.BI bitlog_get_used_count( log )
Returns the total number of bits currently set in the log in
.I O(1)
time.
.TP
.BI bitlog_clear_all( log )
Resets all data words in the backing buffer to 0 and clears all internal cursors 
and metrics.
.SH COMPILATION
The functions are implemented with internal linkage using the
.B static
keyword. The library is intended to be included directly within standard C files. 
For maximum performance, compile with:
.PP
.RS
.B clang -O3 -flto
.RE
.PP
This configuration allows the compiler to inline runtime operations aggressively 
and optimize away unused functions via Link-Time Optimization.
.SH CONFORMING TO
.B C99
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR assert (3)